 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to imposing an additional two percent\noccupancy tax in the county of Onondaga",
    "basePrintNo": "S7789",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7789-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1202-a, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7789\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to imposing an additional two\npercent occupancy tax in the county of Onondaga\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo increase the Onondaga occupancy tax from 5% to 7% on the per diem\nrental room rate.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 1 of section 1202-a of the tax law to\nincrease the Onondaga occupancy tax by 2%.\n\nSection two provides that this act shall take effect on the first day of\nthe month next succeeding the date that it was enacted.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill adds a small increase to the Onondaga occupancy tax rate as\nrequested by the Onondaga County Legislature. The additional funding\nwill be used to promote and enhance local tourism and support small\nbusinesses.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first day of the month next succeeding\nthe date on which it shall have become law.\n",
